{"id": "EUVD-2026-98888", "enisaUuid": "9d5760cd-31a8-3834-94d5-30cf4ec21f04", "description": "Makunet maku-boot 4.3.0 through 5.0.0 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read mail and SMS configurations by calling /sys/mail/config/list and /sys/sms/config/list without the required authority checks. Attackers can retrieve unmasked SMTP passwords and Aliyun, Tencent Cloud, Qiniu or Huawei Cloud access keys, and abuse /sys/mail/config/send to send mail to arbitrary recipients.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T16:53:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T22:19:01", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/maku-boot-mail-sms-config-bfla", "https://github.com/makunet/maku-boot/blob/4cd202b037e2ac47e366d4b0691fb387c764d308/maku-boot-system/src/main/java/net/maku/system/controller/SysMailConfigController.java#L53-L59", "https://github.com/makunet/maku-boot/blob/4cd202b037e2ac47e366d4b0691fb387c764d308/maku-boot-system/src/main/java/net/maku/system/controller/SysMailConfigController.java#L79-L84", "https://github.com/makunet/maku-boot/blob/4cd202b037e2ac47e366d4b0691fb387c764d308/maku-boot-system/src/main/java/net/maku/system/controller/SysSmsConfigController.java#L53-L59", "https://github.com/makunet/maku-boot/releases/tag/v5.0.0", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/makunet-maku-boot-4.3.0-through-5.0.0-missing-authorization-via-mail-and-sms-config-endpoints"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110123", "GHSA-h693-8653-564c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "fa79f6ad-8136-3a5a-89ef-008432317c42", "product": {"name": "maku-boot", "vendor": {"name": "unspecified"}}, "product_version": "4.3.0 \u22645.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1fd5f564-890a-3fc2-b296-834c6c2da061", "vendor": {"name": "makunet"}}], "isExploited": false}